cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build on this thesis, please cite it as below."
title: "Encajes entre nociones de forcing"
abstract: >-
  Bachelor's thesis on advanced set theory: a study of embeddings between
  forcing notions and the generic extensions they produce. The work develops
  complete and dense embeddings, the quotient construction Q/G, composition
  of forcing notions, and the result that every countable atomless forcing
  notion contains Cohen forcing as a dense suborder. Concludes with
  separative quotients and two distinct ways to densely embed any partial
  order into a separative one.
type: thesis
